  "notes": "Source: 2025-2026 Aultman College Catalog (Summer 2025), official Associate of Applied Science in Diagnostic Medical Sonography curriculum plan (Fall — Semester One through Spring — Semester Five, 65 credit hours total), verified via aultmancollege.edu 2026-10-01. The catalog publishes the plan term-by-term; it is cohort-based and sequential, and progression requires following the curriculum plan sequence and meeting all prerequisites. Prerequisites and corequisites transcribed verbatim from the catalog's course-description section (DMS 116/117/212: 'Prerequisites: BIO 207/L, DMS 101, DMS 112, and DMS 115'). Course titles use the program-table wording, which differs slightly from the course-description headings in a few cases (e.g., 'Vascular I' vs 'Vascular Sonography I', 'Sonographic Capstone' vs 'Sonography Capstone'). The course-description section lists DMS 216 Echocardiography II as 2 credits, but the official curriculum plan lists it as 3 credits with a Fall — Semester Four total of 11 (3+3+3+2); the plan value (3) is recorded here. Program total: minimum 65 credit hours (35 major + 30 foundational education).",
